     is required by `numbers`. The defect, if any, is in the source pair, not in nb.
  2. a#10 — restoring «som regel» would reverse RULEBOOK-FIX R3, which the supervisor applied
     deliberately to remove the inherited result claim. Kept R3's wording; added only «fengsel».
  3. a#19 / b#16 — the U+200B lines and the plain-paragraph Q16–Q20 are pinned to the Korean source
     by the checker (`ZWSP` and `headings`). They cannot be "cleaned" per locale.
  4. a#31 / b#8 — Norwegian would indeed use a space, but the checker cannot parse it and
     ACCEPTED-ROUND already skips this row class.
  5. b#34 — the heading skip 5 → 7 → 8 exists in the Korean and English sources.
  6. b#7 suggested «direktører» for 董事, which contradicts a#4 in the same round («*direktør* is an
